{"Shutdown ordering can lose offset commits - commit thread is joined before workers are shut down, so offsets completed by workers after the final commit iteration are never committed, causing unnecessary message reprocessing on restart": 0.8981768488883972, "Unbounded queues provide no backpressure despite docstring claim - queue.Queue() is created without maxsize, so put() never blocks and memory grows unboundedly if workers are slow": 0.933635413646698, "get_committable_offsets iterates O(max_offset - min_offset) per partition - the range loop iterates every integer between lowest and highest tracked offset, which is inefficient for sparse offsets": 0.6255218982696533, "queue.ShutDown caught during processing leaves remaining queued items with uncommittable offsets - if queue.ShutDown is raised during result_processor() or sentry_sdk.start_transaction(), items already enqueued will never have complete_offset() called, permanently blocking commits past those offsets": 0.7683116793632507}